      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I just want to expand on what was said regarding accessibility requests on point 4. I'm the friend that Spectral was referring to. I won't bore with you the details, but I injured myself in 2018 and have had great difficulty getting back to normal. The muscles in my hands are not atrophied, but they are incredibly sensitive and get sore very quickly. \nTo put it simply, although I've tried VRchat on and off, gestures add a lot of various motions that my fingers might be able to do once or twice, but not repeatedly. Its been one of the biggest barriers to entry for me. On the other hand, my thumbs are much more solid, and even trigger use with my index finger would be considerably easier since it would be less taxing on those muscles.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
